1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
How to open a UB

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Marlboro's Designer supports you to open a UB according to the shape of the board.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Here I added a seat in advance.

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Right-click on the 2D board window or 3D window title bar, and then select Open UB Editor.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
You can see that there are two labels at the bottom of the 2D window.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:29,000
You can quickly switch between the 2D window and the UB editor window again.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Right-click on the blank area in the UB window, and you can place the UB in the 2D board.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Tips 1. Before you start editing UB, it is best to place the UB in the 2D board first.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
This is to have the correct ratio between UBs and to organize the UB position.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
You can use the automatic UB fill tool in the upper left corner.

11
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,000
Fill here, enter the value, and determine the distance between the UB pieces.

12
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Select the optimized layout, and press and hold to select whether to allow rotation and whether to set the shrink ratio.

13
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:06,000
It will automatically move the selected UB pieces to the appropriate size and place them in the first line.

14
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Select the UB pieces and right-click.

15
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:18,000
You can turn the UB pieces horizontally or vertically, and you can also align them.

16
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Then right-click and place the UB pieces at 0-1.

17
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Enter the number in the dialog box at the bottom.

18
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Determine the distance between the UB pieces and the edge of the UB frame.

19
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,000
This operation will mix the selected UB pieces together and fill it to the first UB line.

20
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:36,000
Tips 2. If you want to edit the UB on the back and side of the board,

21
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
First, change the texture display on the 3D window to the Rumi texture surface.

22
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:44,000
You must change it here to identify the UB on the back and side.

23
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Select the board, adjust the height, increase the thickness, zoom, and mm.

24
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,000
This will determine the width of the UB on the side.

25
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Pull the element edit button to the bottom.

26
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Open the UB expansion bar and select the UB you want to appear.

27
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Tips 3. Select the UB on the back and side.

28
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,000
At this time, the UB on the back and side has appeared in the UB editor.

29
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,000
The UB on the back is defaulted to overlap with the UB on the front.

30
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,000
The UB on the side is defaulted to squeeze out along the edge of the UB on the front.

31
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Tips 2. Try the distance between the UB pieces and the distance between the UB pieces and the UB frame.

32
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:16,000
The two numbers written below should be greater than the thickness of the fabric.

33
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:20,000
In case of opening the UB on the side, there will be a cross overlap between the UB pieces.

34
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,000
If you plan to use different materials on the front and back,

35
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,000
press Shift and A to select all the UB pieces on the front.

36
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:31,000
Use the Move UB tool to move the UB on the front to other lines.

37
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Tips 3. Click on the item you want to use.

38
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:39,000
In the property editor, in the property, switch to the back cover page.

39
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:42,000
To cancel the selection of materials with the same material on the front,

40
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,000
you can click on the material on the back here.

41
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Tips 4. Select the material on the side.

42
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Tips 5. Select the material on the side.

43
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
At this time, the UB editing is basically complete.

44
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Click on the small ball in the upper left corner to see the different types of postage effects again.

45
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Tips 6. Use the baking pattern tool to bake and save the postage you need.

46
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Tips 7. Use the UB quick photo tool to screenshot and save the UB quick photo you need.

47
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:20,000
That's all for today.

48
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:21,000
Thanks for watching.

49
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
That's all for today.

50
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:25,000
See you in the next video.

